    <briefdescription>
<para>Exponential-splines fitting method. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Fits a discount function to the exponential form <formula id="396">\[ d(t) = \sum_{i=1}^9 c_i \exp^{-kappa i t} \]</formula> where the constants <formula id="55">$ c_i $</formula> and <formula id="397">$ \kappa $</formula> are to be determined. See:Li, B., E. DeWetering, G. Lucas, R. Brenner and A. Shapiro (2001): &quot;Merrill Lynch Exponential Spline
       Model.&quot; Merrill Lynch Working Paper</para><para><xrefsect id="caveats_1_caveats000139"><xreftitle>Warning</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>convergence may be slow </para></xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>    </detaileddescription>
